WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:04.130
Young Eddard Stark: As a boy, even I dreamed
sometimes of being not a Stark of Winterfell,

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:08.069
but a Dayne of Starfall.

00:00:08.069 --> 00:00:12.259
Legend has it that the Dornish founder of
House Dayne followed a falling star to where

00:00:12.259 --> 00:00:13.369
it hit the ground.

00:00:13.369 --> 00:00:15.619
And there, he raised his castle.

00:00:15.619 --> 00:00:21.780
A fantastic story, I know, but House Dayne
has a relic to prove it.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:23.180
Dawn.

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:29.280
The most famous sword in Westeros.Forged from
the fallen star's cold heart, and as strong

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.870
and sharp as Valyrian steel.

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:37.480
Many Houses have ancestral swords passed from
father to oldest son, like my own family's

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:38.930
Ice.

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:42.589
But Dawn doesn't pass to the Lord of Starfall
by right.

00:00:42.589 --> 00:00:46.500
To wield Dawn, a knight of their House must
first be deemed worthy.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:50.920
It doesn't matter if he's the lord, a younger
brother, or a distant cousin.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:55.989
If none are found to be worthy, the blade
stays on the mantle in Starfall until the

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:57.179
next generation.

00:00:57.179 --> 00:01:00.289
But Dawn hasn't rested there often.

00:01:00.289 --> 00:01:03.809
From House Dayne have risen some of the greatest
warriors in Westeros.

00:01:03.809 --> 00:01:09.540
VorianDayne, who was a king and the greatest
knight in Dorne before he was defeated by

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:11.300
Nymeria.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:16.290
Because of his honor, and his prowess, she
sent him to the Wall in golden fetters and

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:18.720
took his heir as her husband.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:24.100
Joffrey Dayne, who answered Aegon the Conqueror's
demand to submit by invading Aegon's Seven

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:29.380
Kingdoms and marching an army to the gates
of Oldtown, where Aegon had been crowned.

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:34.890
And the greatest of them all: Ser Arthur Dayne.

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:37.750
The Sword of the Morning.

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:43.170
During the reign of the Mad King, a band of
outlaws calling themselves the Kingswood Brotherhood

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:46.750
terrorized the forest outside of King's Landing.

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:51.740
Every force sent after them either returned
empty-handed or vanished into the woods, never

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:53.550
to be seen again.

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:59.960
The king was furious and dispatched Ser Arthur
of his own Kingsguard to deal with the threat.

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:03.960
Ser Arthur didn't put the villagers to the
question or set fire to the woods to smoke

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:07.490
out the Brotherhood, as other forces had done.

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:11.810
He paid the smallfolk for the food his men
ate, brought their grievances to the King,

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:15.910
even won them the right to take a few of the
King's deer during the autumn.

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:19.600
The forest folk had looked to the outlaws
to defend them.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:24.240
But Ser Arthur did more for them than the
outlaws could ever hope to do.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:28.920
When a villager led Ser Arthur and his knights
to the outlaws' secret camp, the Brotherhood,

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:32.120
to their credit, didn't flee.

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:37.240
One of their leaders, the Smiling Knight,
was a madman.

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:39.700
Cruelty and honor jumbled together.

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:42.240
But he didn't know fear.

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:44.980
Not even when Ser Arthur drew Dawn before
him.

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:50.490
Soon, the outlaw's longsword had so many notches
that Ser Arthur stopped to let him fetch a

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:51.580
new one.

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:55.950
The robber knight chose another and then asked
for Dawn.

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:59.470
Ser Arthur replied, "Then you shall have it."

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:03.040
The Smiling Knight never smiled again.

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:05.840
The mad fool.

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:07.650
Dawn is just a sword.

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:09.840
Ser Arthur was the true steel.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:14.020
Strong, brave, and loyal to a fault.

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:18.849
He would never have aided Rhaegar's abduction
of my sister if his vows hadn't compelled

00:03:18.849 --> 00:03:19.849
him.

00:03:19.849 --> 00:03:24.819
And though we fought on opposite sides, I
admired him.

00:03:24.819 --> 00:03:28.560
When I was younger, I wanted to be him.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:29.730
Every boy did.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:33.849
And I killed him.

00:03:33.849 --> 00:03:38.630
Not in single combat, but as he was on his
knees, a dagger in his back.

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:41.520
I'll never forget the look in his eyes.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:44.030
He wasn't angry or betrayed.

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:48.990
He'd done his duty to the last, even though
he found it dishonorable.

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:54.250
And even though he knew what awaited me in
that tower.

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:57.940
Ser Arthur Dayne died the greatest knight
who ever lived.

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:01.690
After Robert's coronation, I returned Dawn
to Starfall.

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:06.410
One day, House Dayne will raise a worthy successor
to Ser Arthur.

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:13.790
Until then, Dawn gathers dust above the fire,
with the dream of every boy in Westeros.

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:20.049
Catelyn Stark: Some houses rise to power through
strength, others through wealth.

00:04:20.049 --> 00:04:23.990
House Frey gained its title through cunning.

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:30.030
Centuries ago, its founder looked at a map
and noticed how the Trident spears the Neck,

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:32.460
cutting off the North from the South.

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:37.750
He realized that a river of gold would flow
to the man who owned the right bridge across

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:38.750
the water.

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:45.020
It took the Freys three generations to complete
their forefather's vision: A massive arch

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:49.889
of smooth grey rock, wide enough for two wagons
to pass abreast.

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:57.120
When they were done, they built high curtain
walls, deep moats, and heavy gates to protect

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:04.380
the approaches and put up squat, ugly, formidable
keeps on either bank: the Twins.

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:10.940
Commanding both road and river with arrow
slits, murder holes, and portcullises, the

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:18.150
Twins ensure that no one crosses without begging
the Freys' leave and paying the Freys' toll.

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:19.580
The plan worked.

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:26.500
The family grew rich and powerful, exacting
gold from lords, merchants, and poor farmers.

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:31.140
A good thing too, given the number of Freys
the bridge has to support.

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:36.150
Whatever the case, House Frey does nothing
so well as survive.

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:41.610
When the ironborn conquered and razed the
Riverlands, the Freys hid in their castle.

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:47.280
When Aegon and House Tully swept the ironborn
back to their islands, the Freys hid in their

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:48.610
castle.

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:54.560
When my ancestor demanded their allegiance
as Aegon's new Lord Paramount of the Trident,

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:58.520
the Freys bent the knee from their castle.

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:03.940
Perhaps then we should not have been surprised
when my father, Lord Hoster Tully, called

00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:08.889
his banners against the Mad King and Lord
Walder didn't answer.

00:06:08.889 --> 00:06:15.330
The Baratheons, Starks, Arryns, and Tullys,
some of the oldest and greatest houses of

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:21.949
Westeros, fought and bled for the cause of
justice while House Frey hid in their castle

00:06:21.949 --> 00:06:23.729
and waited.

00:06:23.729 --> 00:06:28.600
No doubt if Rhaegar had won at the Trident,
Lord Walder would have given him safe passage

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:35.669
into the North to destroy the rest of my husband's
Northern army for a fair price.

00:06:35.669 --> 00:06:41.990
But Rhaegar fell and, lo and behold, the Frey
army appeared to render aid to our already

00:06:41.990 --> 00:06:44.560
victorious forces.

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:50.130
Many sniggered that Lord Walder had been waiting
for his army to come of age, having fielded

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:53.090
it out of his own breeches.

00:06:53.090 --> 00:06:56.791
My own father named him The Late Lord Frey
to the other lords' amusement.

00:06:56.791 --> 00:07:01.370
In many ways, however, Lord Walder was wise.

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:07.729
We had no guarantee of victory and had he
fought with them from the outset and we failed,

00:07:07.729 --> 00:07:11.370
he would have lost the bridge his family was
so proud of.

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:14.419
"More Pride Than Honor."

00:07:14.419 --> 00:07:17.750
those should be the words of House Frey.

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:22.979
Yet part of me wonders if Lord Walder waited
not out of fear but hope.

00:07:22.979 --> 00:07:29.050
That we would be destroyed, leaving him to
assume the my family's place as Lord Paramount

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:30.200
of the Trident.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:34.770
To buy the respect they have always wanted,
but refused to earn.

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:41.020
Randyll Tarly: Most Houses take wild beasts
for their sigils, calling themselves bears,

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:45.520
lions, or stags as if a cloth banner could
make them so.

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:49.100
That isn't the way of House Tarly.

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:54.979
Our sigil is the huntsman pulling his bow,
and it isn't some idle fancy.

00:07:54.979 --> 00:08:00.169
As soon as a son of House Tarly can hold a
spoon, he gets a bow.

00:08:00.169 --> 00:08:05.690
As soon as the boy can sit a horse, his father
takes him on a hunt.

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:12.130
They return with a stag, a buck, a boar, a
brace of pheasant, even if it takes days,

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:18.400
even if it takes a week, even if it takes
the boy's whole life.

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:20.390
Horn Hill is ours.

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:26.360
A fitting home for one of the oldest and most
honorable families of the Reach.

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:33.240
Legend has it that Harlon the Hunter and Herndon
of the Horn, two sons of Garth the Greenhand,

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:41.150
raised the castle in the Age of Heroes, and
shared a home and wife for a hundred years.

00:08:41.150 --> 00:08:44.690
Most of the Great Houses spout such nonsense
about their origins.

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:51.100
At least my family doesn't claim some long-lost
ancient crown, like the rest of them.

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:55.060
House Tarly breeds soldiers, not kings.

00:08:55.060 --> 00:09:00.430
When House Gardener ruled the Reach, we served
them well and loyally.

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:07.390
When House Gardener died, and Aegon gave the
Reach to their stewards, House Tyrell, we

00:09:07.390 --> 00:09:09.870
served them well and loyally.

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:15.790
We know our place, even if the Tyrell women
don't.

00:09:15.790 --> 00:09:22.470
When Aegon's son faced rebellion from the
Vulture King of Dorne, my ancestor, Savage

00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:27.350
Sam Tarly, led the royal forces on a Vulture
Hunt.

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:34.430
Heartsbane, our ancestral Valyrian sword,
and the pride of our House, soon ran red from

00:09:34.430 --> 00:09:37.160
point to hilt with rebel blood.

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:44.810
When Robert Baratheon rebelled against Aerys,
I led the Tyrell van and handed him his only

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:46.829
defeat in the war at Ashford.

